   "bounds": [
    "STEPWISE_RUNTIMES in src/pylike/tarfile.ts lists the two versions. On any other `process.versions.node`, or under a runtime that reports itself as Bun or Deno, reading a gzip container ends in `UnsupportedRuntime` before an engine is made. That is a plain Error, not an archive refusal: no handler of the engine catches it and it carries no public code.",
    "The list is held against the pin: test/unit/port-runtime.test.js and scripts/check-port-ready fail if the version in oracle/versions.yml is not in it. Moving the pin therefore means reading `processChunkSync`, `_close` and `zlibOnError` of the new lib/zlib.js, running the gates on the new Node, and adding the version.",
    "The list is narrower than `engines.node`. The package metadata was not changed; it is what the approved plan states.",
    "The payload digest of the pin could not be compared on the development host, which does not hold inputs/node.tar.gz. The Node 24.14.0 the gates ran on is the binary of the upstream node-v24.14.0-linux-x64.tar.xz (sha256 of the archive 41cd79bb7877c81605a9e68ec4c91547774f46a40c67a17e34d7179ef11729df, of bin/node e237a2839d0cbdc9a9a2adda1a184afc0f5b20306ffbe923af5686550472d8a8)."
   ],
   "evidence": [
